title: Reverting a revision
tags: [[Revert]]
kind: guide
summary: mf log revert <revision> (or --op) writes the inverse at HEAD; plan shows it first; a blocked revert names its blockers, --with-dependents takes them along.

```
mf -n music log revert plan 12          # what it would do — nothing written, no lock
mf -n music log revert 12               # revert revision 12
mf -n music log revert --op 23          # only one of its operations (repeatable)
mf -n music log revert                  # the revision HEAD is in
mf -n music log revert 12 --with-dependents
mf -n music log revert 12 --metadata-only --label "undo the bulk rename"
```

A metadata-only revert asks for nothing: it can itself be reverted, which is the point
of preferring it to a rollback.

''Blocked.'' When a later operation wrote the same cell ([[Operation dependencies]]), the
revert is refused, naming what stands in the way:

```
Cannot revert revision 12: 1 of its 2 operations is blocked.

  op 23  set_field(mfr_path)  on 5f2a1c88…
    blocked by op 91  (rev 40, 2024-01-16 08:04, file_moved mfr_path)

Revert rev 40 first, or pass --op 22 to revert only what is free,
or --with-dependents to revert those 1 operation(s) along with it.
```

`--with-dependents` reverts the whole dependency closure — the target and everything
blocking it, transitively. It always prints the closure's size and asks, because how
much history it pulls in is exactly what the target alone does not tell you (`--force`
skips the question, and does not imply `--with-dependents`).

''Files.'' When the plan needs file actions, the CLI shows it, asks (unless `--force`),
and carries them out under the navigation lock: moving a file back (`--on-move-available`,
default `apply`; `--on-move-unavailable`, default `ask`; an occupied destination goes to
the trash first, so no byte is lost), bringing content back from the trash, or sending
it back there. What it cannot do is simply left out of the revert, and named:

```
Reverted revision 12 as revision 57 (2 operations, 1 file moved).

  op 22  set_field(rating)    5 → 3
  op 23  file_moved(mfr_path) music/new.mp3 → music/old.mp3   (mv)
```

`--metadata-only` leaves out every operation needing a file action.

In the GUI, the `log` panel's `log:revert` reverts what is selected.
